<%# "Mark Complete" action for a non-quiz/non-assignment-submission
    content item - see lessons-view.ejs's own header comment for the real
    request this answers. Reuses canTakeQuiz/quizBasePathLocal/
    quizQueryLocal exactly as the quiz branch does: same portal/per-class
    gate, same base path.

    A real request: "Marking complete on an assignment shouldn't be an
    orange button. It should be a green check mark circle that you can
    click to mark complete and it will say complete very small under the
    check mark." icon-circle (an empty ring) for the clickable not-yet-
    done state; the done state is a plain checkmark (icon-check) inside
    its own filled green circle (.lesson-complete-badge) - a real
    follow-up request: "marking an assignment complete should be a filled
    in green circle with a check mark," rather than icon-check-circle's
    own outline-circle-plus-outline-check look. %>
<div class="lesson-item-complete">
  <% if (item.completed) { %>
    <span class="lesson-complete-check lesson-complete-check-done" aria-label="Completed">
      <span class="lesson-complete-badge"><svg class="icon"><use href="#icon-check"/></svg></span>
      <span class="lesson-complete-label">Complete</span>
    </span>
  <% } else if (canTakeQuiz) { %>
    <form method="POST" action="<%= quizBasePathLocal %>/content/<%= item.id %>/complete<%= quizQueryLocal %>" class="inline-block-form">
      <button type="submit" class="lesson-complete-check" aria-label="Mark complete">
        <svg class="icon"><use href="#icon-circle"/></svg>
        <span class="lesson-complete-label">Mark Complete</span>
      </button>
    </form>
  <% } else { %>
    <span class="hint">Not completed yet</span>
  <% } %>
</div>
